cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Touchstone (Standard or library), please cite both the Standard and the library."
title: "Touchstone"
abstract: >
  Touchstone is a model-independent verification methodology and reference
  implementation for AI-coupled work. The Standard defines eleven measurement
  layers for output profiling (Section 5) and five layers for specification
  compliance verification (Section 6), all designed to operate without
  depending on AI models to judge AI outputs. The library is the canonical
  reference implementation; v0.1 ships Section 5 measurement only,
  empirically validated against the published EXP-081 adversarial-validity
  finding (Cohen's d=-5.43 reproduction) and the EXP-095 grounding
  decomposition corpus. Section 6 (Specification Compliance) is reserved
  for a future release.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Clarethium"
    website: "https://clarethium.com"
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://touchstone.clarethium.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Clarethium/touchstone"
keywords:
  - artificial-intelligence
  - ai-evaluation
  - ai-output-verification
  - fabrication-detection
  - source-grounding
  - structural-verification
  - model-independent
  - touchstone-standard
references:
